{
  "_about": "Controlled vocabulary for the `dynasty` field. Pure lexical normalisation: it maps spelling and qualifier variants onto one canonical label and NOTHING ELSE. No dates, regions or attributions are asserted here — those would be facts, and facts need sources (CLAUDE.md rule 2 / guardrail G2).",
  "_usage": "scripts/normalize-vocab.mjs reads this to report drift; scripts/merge-batches.mjs should apply it to incoming records so new batches land normalised.",
  "_measured": "941 records carried 313 distinct dynasty values, 246 of them appearing exactly once. One wave of 253 records added 99 new values, so this must be applied at ingest, not swept afterwards.",
  "_note_field": "Where an alias carries a real sub-distinction (ruling house, 'legacy', 'attributed'), `note` preserves it rather than discarding it. The canonical label is for faceting; the note is for display.",
